repository-code: "https://github.com/Kesav2k04/ugaa-research"
abstract: >
  We document a token-extraction artifact in the reference POPE
  evaluator: it compares logits at vocabulary IDs 3582 and 1217, which
  LLaVA-1.5-7B never produces as the first generated token after the
  ASSISTANT: prompt suffix. The model instead emits the
  space-prefixed forms (IDs 3869 and 1939). Under a corrected
  eight-token rule the LLaVA-1.5-7B baseline rises by 6.13 F1 points
  on the POPE adversarial split, a gap larger than the headline gain
  claimed by several recent inference-time methods. The repository
  contains the diagnostic, the 9,000 prediction records, and a paper
  describing the artifact and its arithmetic.
